## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical handling of dynamic per-tenant quotas, fairness under contention, and runtime reconfiguration in a streaming context.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant concurrency caps
- Fair scheduling across tenants
- Global bounded queues and backpressure
- Runtime cap reconfiguration without downtime
- Correctness: ordering within tenant and starvation avoidance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code sketch: minimal enqueue/consume with per-tenant controls
class Scheduler {
  constructor(Q, tenants) {
    this.globalQ = new BoundedQueue(Q);
    this.tenants = tenants; // map<tenantId, {C_t, sem, queues}>
  }
  enqueue(task) {
    // block if globalQ full
    this.globalQ.enqueue(task);
  }
  workerLoop() {
    while (true) {
      for (const t of this.tenants.values()) {
        if (t.semaphore.tryAcquire()) {
          const x = t.queues[type].dequeue();
          if (x) process(x);
        }
      }
      // optional backoff
    }
  }
  updateCap(tenantId, newCap) {
    const t = this.tenants.get(tenantId);
    t.semaphore.updateLimit(newCap);
  }
}
```

